  "body": "### What happens\n\nThe post-merge gate on main `4f4edcf35` failed twice (run 43620716239, attempts 1 and 2). The cause is the runner, not a test.\n\n- Attempt 1: the sim suites ran. After them, sccache failed: \"failed to execute compile ... Failed to read response header\". motion, app, ui and clippy then failed in 0 s.\n- Attempt 2: the gate failed at once. `sccache rustc -vV` exited 2: \"Failed to send data to or receive data from server\". No test ran.\n\n### Expected\n\nThe gate builds either way. When the sccache server is dead, the build falls back to plain rustc, or the runner starts the sccache server again before the gate.\n\n### Evidence\n\n- Run: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/actions/runs/43620716239\n- Artifact `gate-logs-post-merge-43620716239-2` holds the 385-byte failure log.\n- The runner sets `RUSTC_WRAPPER` to sccache per issue #1413's setup.\n\n### Done means\n\nOne green `cargo xtask gate batch` run on the self-hosted runner after the fix. The runner keeps the sccache server alive, or `cargo xtask gate` disables the wrapper when sccache answers an error.\n\nRelated: #900 (sccache opt-in), #1451 (the post-merge gate).\n",
